# The lockfile IS committed now.
#
# It was ignored on the reasoning that a library's lock is ignored by consumers —
# true, but that is not the only job it does. Without one, `npm install` crashes
# on some npm versions ("Cannot read properties of null (reading 'edgesOut')") and
# every CI run resolves a slightly different dependency tree, so a failure cannot
# be reproduced. It also gives Dependabot/audit a pinned surface to report on.
